Include relations.

Let R, S be relation.

Lemma: R is symmetric and S is symmetric implies (R ∩ S) is symmetric.
Proof:
    Assume R is symmetric and S is symmetric.
    Assume (R ∩ S)[x,y].
    Then R[x,y] and S[x,y].
    Then R[y,x] by symmetry.
    Then S[y,x] by symmetry.
    Then (R ∩ S)[y,x].
    Hence (R ∩ S) is symmetric.
qed.
